{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgdYquNP6Fugqmg7Zx73y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The report on Thrive Holdings' acquisition of ADT was updated after publication to add two details: that Thrive Holdings is a holding company, and that ADT already partners with Apple and Google and is expected to keep doing so. Both details change how the deal reads.\n\nThe first concerns what kind of buyer ADT now has. Thrive Holdings was spun out of Josh Kushner's venture firm Thrive Capital, and its stated mission is to own companies long-term and revitalize them with AI. It says it holds more than 75 of them. OpenAI is an investor and partner, providing those companies with AI models, technology and forward-deployed engineers. The deal, announced Thursday, is priced at $10 per share, about $7.6 billion in equity, with a total enterprise value of $15.3 billion according to ADT. A holding company paying that much with the stated intent of keeping the business indicates that Thrive plans to run ADT for the long term, with OpenAI's resources inside it.\n\nThe second detail concerns ADT's place in a market that large technology companies are moving into. Apple has just launched home security and smart home products with LG and Schneider Electric, and Amazon has added new AI-powered cameras to its smart home line. ADT's continuing partnerships with Apple and Google mean it will work with those platforms while building AI products under an OpenAI-backed owner. Apple is now also selling its own security products.\n\nWhat the companies have described is a direction. The press release says ADT \"will form the foundation of Thrive Holdings' smart home security business,\" and both sides say they plan to invest and release new products. None have been named, so how ADT's new AI products will fit alongside its Apple and Google partnerships remains unanswered."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1013,"cache_read_input_tokens":4893,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1013},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"611c2f65-ce1a-4fdd-97bb-2cc127751ac9","uuid":"7a260d7a-6d65-48aa-bc71-9b7c6af97b46","timestamp":"2026-11-02T05:29:00.517Z","request_id":"req_011CgdYquAxk23LpdHjYim5L"}
